  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="80.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 80.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="80.1" corresp="#wit-g-a">⁊ forgá ælc man minne huntnoð locehwær ic hit gefriðod wylle habban, be fullan wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="80.1" corresp="#wit-a">⁊ forga elc man minne huntað, lochwær ic hit gefriðod habben wille, be fullan wite.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="80.1" corresp="#wit-q">Et abstineat omnis homo á uenariis meis, ubicumque pacem eis haberi uolo, super plenam witam.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="80.1" corresp="#wit-b">⁊ forgá ælc man minne huntnoð lochwar ic hit gefriðod wille habban [on minon agenan], be fullan wite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">But everyone, under pain of incurring the full penalty, shall avoid hunting on my preserves, wherever they may be.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Aber jedermann vermeide meine Jagd, wo immer ich sie [mit Forstbann] umfriedet haben will, bei vollem Strafgelde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But let every man avoid my hunting, wherever I wish to have it protected [by forest-ban], on pain of the full fine.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann prints in a footnote some additions on fishponds and dogs (80.1a–b) which MS T of the Quadripartitus adds here, about 1220.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
